    "report": "Messaging and Notifications no longer read the machine's time. The change is committed on `main` as `09d93b0`, not pushed. I did not start a server.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging:**\n  - The wiring, the StartConversation and SendMessage handlers, and the ReportMessage handler all take the clock from `messagingWiring`. I removed the `() => new Date()` defaults.\n  - ReportMessage previously let the domain default `reportedAt` to the machine's time. It now passes the clock.\n  - `Conversation.start`, `send` and `report` require the time they record.\n- **Notifications:**\n  - `NoticeWindow.admit`, `MessageNoticeOwing.owe` and `Notice.accept` require the time.\n  - `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler` and `NoticeDelivery` take the clock. `notificationsWiring` takes it as a parameter, and `createApplication` passes the existing clock.\n- Specs that relied on the old defaults now pass a fixed instant.\n\n**Verification**\n- `yarn typecheck`, `eslint` and `prettier --check` on the changed files all pass.\n- `yarn check:conventions` passes.\n- `yarn test` on the Messaging and Notifications folders: 22 suites, 103 tests, all pass.\n- The three Bootstrap e2e suites that exercise messages and notices pass, 48 tests.\n- A grep finds no `new Date()`, `Date.now()` or defaulted clock left in either context's code. Two e2e specs still read `Date.now()`, but only to compute expected values in the tests.\n\n**Decisions and things to know**\n- **Behaviour with an offset:** with `CLOCK_OFFSET_DAYS` at 0, nothing a client sees changes. With an offset set, a report's stored `reportedAt` is now the offset time, as the project guide requires for any stored time.\n- **Test instants:** the specs use fixed dates (`2026-11-17` in the Messaging domain specs, `2027-05-01` in the Notifications specs), not the clock.\n- **Test runner:** plain `npx jest` fails on every suite because the project needs `--experimental-vm-modules`. I ran the tests through `yarn test`, which sets it.\n- **Left alone:** Accounts' two-factor clock (`() => new Date()` in `createApplication`) is deliberately on the machine's time per its own comment. It is outside Messaging and Notifications, so I did not touch it.",
